line3\\n\", Pipeline: cat data.txt | sponge data.txt'\n    40→    inputs:\n    41→      args: [\"data.txt\"]\n    42→      stdin: \"content of data.txt (fed via 'cat data.txt')\"\n    43→      env: []\n    44→    normalization: none\n    45→    expected:\n    46→      exit_code: 0\n    47→      stdout_structure: 'expected file data.txt contains \"line1\\nline2\\nline3\\n\"'\n    48→      stderr: \"\"\n    49→    traces:\n    50→      - prd007-sponge R1.1\n    51→      - prd007-sponge R2.5\n    52→\n    53→  - name: sponge_passthrough_stdout\n    54→    description: No output filename; stdin content appears on stdout.\n    55→    inputs:\n    56→      args: []\n    57→      stdin: \"hello world\\n\"\n    58→      env: []\n    59→    normalization: none\n    60→    expected:\n    61→      exit_code: 0\n    62→      stdout: \"hello world\\n\"\n    63→      stderr: \"\"\n    64→    traces:\n    65→      - prd007-sponge R4.1\n    66→      - prd007-sponge R4.3\n    67→\n    68→  - name: sponge_append_mode\n    69→    description: '-a flag prepends original file content before stdin content. Setup: existing.txt contains \"original line\\n\"'\n    70→    inputs:\n    71→      args: [\"-a\", \"existing.txt\"]\n    72→      stdin: \"appended line\\n\"\n    73→      env: []\n    74→    normalization: none\n    75→    expected:\n    76→      exit_code: 0\n    77→      stdout_structure: 'expected file existing.txt contains \"original line\\nappended line\\n\"'\n    78→      stderr: \"\"\n    79→    traces:\n    80→      - prd007-sponge R3.1\n    81→      - prd007-sponge R3.3\n    82→\n    83→  - name: sponge_append_mode_no_existing_file\n    84→    description: '-a with a non-existent output file behaves as default mode (creates new file). Setup: newfile.txt does not exist'\n    85→    inputs:\n    86→      args: [\"-a\", \"newfile.txt\"]\n    87→      stdin: \"new content\\n\"\n    88→      env: []\n    89→    normalization: none\n    90→    expected:\n    91→      exit_code: 0